{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat","id":1119539,"title":"A possibly rather stupid question concerning Duat...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-23T09:18:34-07:00","id":1119539,"title":"A possibly rather stupid question concerning Duat...","content":"Is Duat in the Underworld? Or is it something altogether different? If they're the same, could Sin-Eaters theoretically reach Duat? If they're not the same, then by what criteria do some souls descend to the Underworld, while others go to Duat?<br /> <br /> I apologize for what may well be a rather stupid question, especially if it's been spelled out clearly somewhere and I just didn't see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T10:40:04-07:00","id":1119565,"title":"","content":"Duat's location is left a bit ambiguous. It might be in the Underworld, though the books also hint that the realm is one of the Lower Depths. I think it's one of those things that's going to depend on the needs of any given chronicle.<br /> <br /> If any Sin-Eaters do manage to get there, the Judges are going to be pissed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T10:53:48-07:00","id":1119569,"title":"","content":"It's not the slightest bit ambiguous. Duat is <i>not</i> in the Underworld. It <i>is</i> a Lower Depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T11:00:17-07:00","id":1119572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1119569#post1119569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the slightest bit ambiguous. Duat is <i>not</i> in the Underworld. It <i>is</i> a Lower Depth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, Dave! I appreciate the quick response!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T05:38:27-07:00","id":1119851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat#post1119539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're not the same, then by what criteria do some souls descend to the Underworld, while others go to Duat?</div> </div> </div> </div>The beings going to the Underworld are ghosts, not souls. The confusion comes from the poetic use of soul to refer to ghosts, but as technical terms in the setting, they're different. (The same happens when Duat is called the Underworld).<br /> <br /> There's actually a bit on ghosts in the Mummy core that tocuhes on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T06:26:52-07:00","id":1123852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1119569#post1119569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the slightest bit ambiguous. Duat is <i>not</i> in the Underworld. It <i>is</i> a Lower Depth.</div> </div> </div> </div> The irony is that that the Underworld doesn't recieve souls, its Not really an afterlife at all, its more like a haunted dimesion that seems like an afterlife, but just for Ghosts. <br /> <br /> But Duat does get souls, its an actual afterlife as well as a Lower Depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T07:31:02-07:00","id":1123871,"title":"","content":"To really through you for a loop, Dark Eras Companion states that Anpu seems to be equal parts Lower Depth (Duat), Supernal, and Underworld. I wonder if all the Iremite gods are like that, if it's just Anpu, or if it came after they fell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T09:29:57-07:00","id":1123902,"title":"","content":"Maybe there was a Pangaea (and Pangaean) equivalent for the Underworld? And it too was Sundered some time? Maybe Duat was cast into the Lower Depths?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T16:36:39-07:00","id":1124077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1123902#post1123902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Duat was cast into the Lower Depths?</div> </div> </div> </div>My Mage knowledge is pretty vague, but isn't a Lower Depth just any realm Mages aren't able to classify under any other existing label? I didn't think it was meant to denote any relative cosmological &quot;space&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm working entirely from second-hand information here, mind you, but I was under the impression that it was a fairly meaningless term. At least for anyone who isn't a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T16:48:03-07:00","id":1124082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124077#post1124077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Mage knowledge is pretty vague, but isn't a Lower Depth just any realm Mages aren't able to classify under any other existing label? I didn't think it was meant to denote any relative cosmological &quot;space&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm working entirely from second-hand information here, mind you, but I was under the impression that it was a fairly meaningless term. At least for anyone who isn't a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure? It doesn't really affect my (wild) supposition, though - maybe &quot;Duat&quot; was once accessible, then became &quot;elsewhere&quot;. It still exists, obviously, but Mages can't access it (or at least survive it if they can). So it goes in the &quot;Lower Depth&quot; bin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T10:25:04-07:00","id":1124360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124077#post1124077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Mage knowledge is pretty vague, but isn't a Lower Depth just any realm Mages aren't able to classify under any other existing label? I didn't think it was meant to denote any relative cosmological &quot;space&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm working entirely from second-hand information here, mind you, but I was under the impression that it was a fairly meaningless term. At least for anyone who isn't a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No.<br /> <br /> It isn't a meaningless classification - it means an otherworldy dimension/place that's lacking some aspect of Fallen reality and consumes it, or has inhabitants that consume it when they break into more solid or ephemeral realms.<br /> <br /> In Duat's case, Sekhem. Also souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T15:01:47-07:00","id":1124489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124360#post1124360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> It isn't a meaningless classification - it means an otherworldy dimension/place that's lacking some aspect of Fallen reality and consumes it, or has inhabitants that consume it when they break into more solid or ephemeral realms.<br /> <br /> In Duat's case, Sekhem. Also souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which also puts A'aru as a Lower Depth, right? Since that's where the souls are meant to (at least originally) end up? I'll note that it's not entirely meaningless, but the general point I was getting at with my previous post (that there's a lot of baggage associated with the phrase &quot;cast into the Lower Depths&quot; as if it were some kind of hell, when it's more a kind of semi-scientific nomenclature) still stands if you can as easily argue both of Mummy's afterlives count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:02:46-07:00","id":1124568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124489#post1124489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which also puts A'aru as a Lower Depth, right? Since that's where the souls are meant to (at least originally) end up? I'll note that it's not entirely meaningless, but the general point I was getting at with my previous post (that there's a lot of baggage associated with the phrase &quot;cast into the Lower Depths&quot; as if it were some kind of hell, when it's more a kind of semi-scientific nomenclature) still stands if you can as easily argue both of Mummy's afterlives count.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the difference. Duat is not the natural destination of souls, its more like a tollbooth on the road that demands payment and sends most people back the way they came before they see the place where souls are supposed to go. A'aru is likely where souls were meant to go, whether its the supernal or elsewhere. Only the Dreams of Avarice and heretic apotheiosists would know. Dust isn't somewhere whole, its a broken, conquered thing.<br /> <br /> Now, an interesting question might be if Anpu is the ghost of Father Wolf. Perhaps the legends of Anpu, protector of the borders between earth and other realms, was the same deity as father wolf? Perhaps Anpu didn't precisely abdicate his throne for Azar so much as witness mages, werewolves, shaniatu, and other things mix things up, and found himself overthrown forcefully?<br /> <br /> <br /> With him gone, the Shaniatu had enough freedom to study enough on between to find one they liked, Duat. There it was, conveniently placed to access souls going onward and upward to the supernal and to a'aru, but also oblivion and the abyss. Then, step two.. then three, profit. Nobody was going anywhere without the strict approval of the Judges, unless they got stuck as restless dead in twilight or the underworld.<br /> <br /> Indeed, if Mummies CAN get to the Underworld (we know Deceived explicitly can't), they might see it as the depths of Neter-Kertet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:14:49-07:00","id":1124574,"title":"","content":"I don't consider A'aru a Lower Depth, if it's even a <i>place </i>anyway.<br /> <br /> Despite it's iconic description of being barren, it represents a heaven, a sort of place of fulfillment, belonging, and rest. To Lower Depth beings A'aru is a place where they have all that they naturally lack and desire. Hell, it might even be our regular ol' fallen world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:16:32-07:00","id":1124576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124568#post1124568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's the difference. Duat is not the natural destination of souls, its more like a tollbooth on the road that demands payment and sends most people back the way they came before they see the place where souls are supposed to go. A'aru is likely where souls were meant to go, whether its the supernal or elsewhere. Only the Dreams of Avarice and heretic apotheiosists would know. Dust isn't somewhere whole, its a broken, conquered thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that from what we know, it was a &quot;broken, conquered thing&quot; before it was broken/conquered. At least if we use the term &quot;Lower Depth&quot; to denote that it is broken.<br /> <br /> More importantly, nothing in Dave's description gave me the impression that a Lower Depth was inherently unnatural (setting aside the fact that it's undoubtedly supernatural). Duat could easily be part of the natural process and still consume aspects of the world. Predators and scavengers are natural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T20:20:24-07:00","id":1124598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124576#post1124576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More importantly, nothing in Dave's description gave me the impression that a Lower Depth was inherently unnatural (setting aside the fact that it's undoubtedly supernatural). Duat could easily be part of the natural process and still consume aspects of the world. Predators and scavengers are natural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Predators and scavengers are part of an ecosystem. The stuff a Lower Depth consumes goes <i>nowhere</i>. The stolen Sekhem of Duat is burnt for temporary relief or used to outfit the Arisen; Ammut's certainly not doing anything with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T22:52:42-07:00","id":1124626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124489#post1124489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which also puts A'aru as a Lower Depth, right? Since that's where the souls are meant to (at least originally) end up? I'll note that it's not entirely meaningless, but the general point I was getting at with my previous post (that there's a lot of baggage associated with the phrase &quot;cast into the Lower Depths&quot; as if it were some kind of hell, when it's more a kind of semi-scientific nomenclature) still stands if you can as easily argue both of Mummy's afterlives count.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, according to the Arisen (not the Awakened), Aa'ru is the Supernal Realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T04:04:51-07:00","id":1124686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124626#post1124626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, according to the Arisen (not the Awakened), Aa'ru is the Supernal Realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you could find some Awakened who would agree, if only because the Awakened are inveterate theory-junkies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T06:58:15-07:00","id":1124743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124598#post1124598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Predators and scavengers are part of an ecosystem. The stuff a Lower Depth consumes goes <i>nowhere</i>. The stolen Sekhem of Duat is burnt for temporary relief or used to outfit the Arisen; Ammut's certainly not doing anything with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What we know of Ammut directly contradicts that. She is presented as a source of Sekhem as well as a consumer of it. Duat is a place where Sekhem is cleansed of its imperfections so that it can return to become life again. Ammut describes herself as being directly involved in that process. Sekhem passes through her and returns to the world, she doesn't keep it forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:45:04-07:00","id":1124770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124360#post1124360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> It isn't a meaningless classification - it means an otherworldy dimension/place that's lacking some aspect of Fallen reality and consumes it, or has inhabitants that consume it when they break into more solid or ephemeral realms.<br /> <br /> In Duat's case, Sekhem. Also souls.</div> </div> </div> </div> Does that make most of the Nameless Gods like Azar, Ra, and so on Supernal beings? <br /> <br /> That might suggest that Aset might be an Archmage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T10:53:25-07:00","id":1124836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124743#post1124743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What we know of Ammut directly contradicts that. She is presented as a source of Sekhem as well as a consumer of it. Duat is a place where Sekhem is cleansed of its imperfections so that it can return to become life again. Ammut describes herself as being directly involved in that process. Sekhem passes through her and returns to the world, she doesn't keep it forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ammut describes herself as <i>wanting to bring the world to eternal silence</i>. She is described in no uncertain terms as an <i>oblivion-goddess</i> and a force of <i>anti-being</i>. She is very directly comparable to the entropy of the universe and the promise of the bargain she accepted to let the world keep existing was that she would receive a portion of the world's Sekhem <i>to feed her forever after</i>.<br /> <br /> She explicitly does not need the things she takes and the only place where she's put forward as an engine of the universe rather than a threat to be appeased is in Book of the Deceived, where those ideas are forwarded by Ammut herself or Azar as the voice of the Judges, both speaking to an audience whose eventual sobriquet does not speak well for their veracity.<br /> <br /> &quot;What we know of Ammut&quot; is that every source that speaks about her uses the language of finality in relation to her consumption except for the explicitly probably-unreliable account of <i>one of the Deceived</i>, who suspects she lied to them and puts forth no reason for her not to have done so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-04-2017, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:08:35-07:00","id":1125066,"title":"","content":"The two statements are not mutually exclusive. She <i>wants</i> to bring about eternal silence. She is bound by the Law. So she doesn't, instead being compelled to purify Sekhem so that it might return to the world.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I always find the &quot;Book of the Deceived information comes from an unreliable narrator&quot; to be a terribly weak argument. I like to think the game's writers wrote that information for a reason, I usually don't take seriously the argument that the writers put down information with the intent that it be ignored. We aren't telling a narrative where the unreliable narration can be used to set up or mask an upcoming twist or reveal. The technique is still useful in the RPG game book format, principally as a way to canonically justify individual GMs having different takes on the backstory of Irem or the origins of the Shan'iatu or the Deceived, as appropriate to their specific game. It could be a good way of revealing more about the characters involved, so long as we know they are lying and are able to deduce more about the characters based on what they lie about. But we don't know for certain that Ammut is lying (the only lie we see directly called out as such in the Book's own narration is that of the identity of the narrator), and the revelation that Ammut lies is no revelation since that's basically why we have Shuankhsen. You're welcome to believe that she is, allowing people to believe whatever they want is presumably the whole point of writing that chapter from an unreliable perspective, but believing that she tells the truth expands the game in a far more meaningful way in my view. Positioning the force of entropy as an essential driving force of life in the universe (a necessary evil, for sure) is interesting given the context of the game as being about unchanging immortals clinging to what they once were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 08-04-2017, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T21:01:39-07:00","id":1125079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124770#post1124770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that make most of the Nameless Gods like Azar, Ra, and so on Supernal beings?<br /> <br /> That might suggest that Aset might be an Archmage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it might suggest that the notoriously ignorant Arisen actually have no idea what A'aru might possibly be and have simply used the Awakened's cosmology as their most relatable explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T21:25:15-07:00","id":1125086,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing some of this, and more, will be covered in the Crossover book.<br /> <br /> So someone might get their fandom hurt.<br /> <br /> But you shouldn't let that keep you from doing what you want to do in, or feels right for, your game. Have fun with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-05-2017, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T17:05:04-07:00","id":1125730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124770#post1124770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does that make most of the Nameless Gods like Azar, Ra, and so on Supernal beings?<br /> <br /> That might suggest that Aset might be an Archmage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is a fairly diminishing explanation to assume the truth is as simple as that, even if there is never an official stance on it (and I doubt even the Crossover Chronicles will care too much about such details, since nailing down setting mysteries in favor of one or other line is not something that would be conductive to a more interesting book).<br /> <br /> The Mutapa Empire Dark Era avoids settling down on many of these things and gives more approximations of how each splat might understand the other through the lenses of their own world and magic. As an example from it, Anpu cannot normally be magically scrutinized, but if he allows it then a mage would register him simultaneously as a Supernal being aligned with the Death arcanum, a native of the Underworld, and a being from the Lower Depths, none offering a complete explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T19:57:58-07:00","id":1125767,"title":"","content":"Why can't gods be of more than one realm? Maybe Anpu is a Supernal entity that now lairs in Duat; maybe he's a creature of the Lower Depths that's 'ascended' in some manner. And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T21:56:46-07:00","id":1125793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1125767#post1125767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't gods be of more than one realm? Maybe Anpu is a Supernal entity that now lairs in Duat; maybe he's a creature of the Lower Depths that's 'ascended' in some manner. And so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>So here's the brilliance of the way Anpu was described to Mages: how it works is a mystery. <br /> <br /> What you suggest is certainly one possibility. Since those scenarios defy the normal rules for Supernal Beings (which cannot exist in the Fallen World indefinitely) a Storyteller would have to come up with an explaination for how Supernal!Anpu can exist in the Fallen World and why he registers as being from the additional realms.<br /> <br /> There are other possibilities though. The way Anpu was described leaves open the possiblity that he is from beyond a Mage's normal understanding and the confused Symbols of Anpu are the closest representation their worldview has for what he really is. Since Anpu is a major aspect of Mummy's mythology, that possibility is important, since it leaves Mummy and Mage canonically codominant. Neither cosmology overrides the other. They exist simaltaniously.<br /> <br /> If the answer to Anpu's existence was that he was Supernal, that takes all for the mystery out of it and it causes Mage's mythology to dominate Mummy's. That wouldn't sit well with fans and it takes half the fun out of things. This way, you can have one interpretation, I can have another, and someone else can have a third. If they all explain why Anpu can exist in these three states at the same time, they are all equally valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:21:26-07:00","id":1126038,"title":"","content":"I never understood the complaints people have concerning the CofD's games 'dominating' each others' mythoses. I have absolutely no problem with Anpu being Supernal, with the Exarchs ruling the universe, <i>or</i> 'one mythology overruling the other'. Then again, I'm the guy who freely did crossovers between different oWoD gamelines with nary a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T17:57:33-07:00","id":1126124,"title":"","content":"Because it undermines the individual, unique narrative weight of each game, and supplants it with a game that I probably don't give a shit about or own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T22:59:39-07:00","id":1126196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1126038#post1126038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never understood the complaints people have concerning the CofD's games 'dominating' each others' mythoses. I have absolutely no problem with Anpu being Supernal, with the Exarchs ruling the universe, <i>or</i> 'one mythology overruling the other'. Then again, I'm the guy who freely did crossovers between different oWoD gamelines with nary a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine at you own table or for individual games, but it would be pretty unequivocally terrible if it was set up that way in books or RAW.<br /> Reseru summed it up well.<br /> I should be able to run a game where the Exarchs are simply another name or tool for the Judges if I want to <i>without</i> having to break from Mummy canon - and since this would be a Mummy game, Mage's core matters less. If the Exarchs as tools of the Judges was core-book, though - that'd be pretty frustrating for Mage players and Mummy players alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T03:24:49-07:00","id":1126241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1124489#post1124489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which also puts A'aru as a Lower Depth, right? Since that's where the souls are meant to (at least originally) end up? I'll note that it's not entirely meaningless, but the general point I was getting at with my previous post (that there's a lot of baggage associated with the phrase &quot;cast into the Lower Depths&quot; as if it were some kind of hell, when it's more a kind of semi-scientific nomenclature) still stands if you can as easily argue both of Mummy's afterlives count.</div> </div> </div> </div>A'aru seems to be the Supernal, what with the Book of Names/Ages and what not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T05:31:13-07:00","id":1126266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1126241#post1126241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A'aru seems to be the Supernal, what with the Book of Names/Ages and what not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Scroll of Ages? That was a concept believed in by the Sesha-Hebsu specifically, and so far as I know never associated with A'aru. It was more of a cosmic principle/philosophy than anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T11:11:15-07:00","id":1126382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1126266#post1126266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scroll of Ages? That was a concept believed in by the Sesha-Hebsu specifically, and so far as I know never associated with A'aru. It was more of a cosmic principle/philosophy than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, the Scroll of Ages is mentioned as a &quot;thing&quot; in Dreams of Avarice, being contained in A'aru and which contains all names of all things. It seems to be more than a mere &quot;concept&quot; used by the guilds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T16:12:03-07:00","id":1126495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1126382#post1126382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, the Scroll of Ages is mentioned as a &quot;thing&quot; in Dreams of Avarice, being contained in A'aru and which contains all names of all things. It seems to be more than a mere &quot;concept&quot; used by the guilds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, it's been a while since I read Dreams of Avarice. I had forgotten that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T10:38:14-07:00","id":1126766,"title":"","content":"I had always assumed that there were 3 flavors of reality:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Realms that are complete (ie the Fallen Realm (physical+Shadow+Twilight+Supernal+dream-space (Always kind of seen those three as always occupying the same &quot;space&quot;... ish... or something)</li> <li>Side Realms that are connected like twigs/branches to the tree (Hedge/Mirror Realm, Time blips, Bolt Holes, various pocket Dimensions)</li> <li>And the Lower Depth Realms that are missing a fundamental &quot;thing&quot; and hunger it (Faerie (conflict), Hell (from the source book), Supernal, Abyss, Underworld (Plasm/ghosts), Duat (Sekhem), ETC)</li> </ol>I've gone back and forth whether the Supernal is actually a Lower Depth (missing realities for its symbols) or just another layer to the complete realm (as the counterpart to the physicality of what the symbols represent.<br /> <br /> <br /> Does that still work w/ what Dave said on here? This is just how I've always seen it. (well not always, but more recently I mean.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T10:48:14-07:00","id":1126770,"title":"","content":"Well, the Supernal isn't a place in the usual meaning. It's possible to enter the Supernal, but you do so as a set of symbols and you're almost guaranteed to dissolve into these symbols and not return. Also, it doesn't really lack anything. It requires the material to embody its symbols, but that's similar to the Shadow that requires the material to provide Resonances.<br /> The Underworld isn't a Lower Depth either. It's true that it sucks in ghosts, but it naturally generates Essence (which is what becomes Plasm when ghosts uses Manifestations) and isn't difficult at all to enter. Any mortal with the right knowledge can enter any naturally occuring Graveyard Gate with relative ease without any supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T11:15:10-07:00","id":1126780,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, Then I think the Supernal is prolly just as much a part of this realm as the Shadow or Twilight is. <br /> <br /> If it is true that the Underworld isn't a Lower Depth then I would likely place it in a similar grouping of half-realms like the Hedge. On the ease of getting to a realm, I posit that ease wouldn't necessarily preclude a realm from being a Lower Depth. Could be it's just &quot;close to the surface&quot; as it were. It's close in proximity to ours. All the same, hearing that it makes it's own energy and doesn't seem to really be hungry for anything and that it just... is would make it like a half step like the Hedge. A twig/branch of the tree but not really separate and not really one and the same from the main realm. <br /> <br /> And if it's neither than my whole idea on how it all works is wrong ^.^ and that's fine too. Still tho, this makes sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T13:22:16-07:00","id":1126822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1126766#post1126766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've gone back and forth whether the Supernal is actually a Lower Depth (missing realities for its symbols) or just another layer to the complete realm (as the counterpart to the physicality of what the symbols represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>We all have different ways of connecting the cosmology, but grouping the Supernal with the Lower Depths makes <i>no</i> sense. They're literally <i>defined</i> as opposites of each other: the Supernal is complete and the Lower Depths are empty or missing something essential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T19:43:10-07:00","id":1126935,"title":"","content":"The underworld cannot be a lower depth, part of the definition of a lower depth is that normal people cannot possibly leave them because of their Lack. Arcadia also is unlikely to be a lower depth because of the same reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T21:49:00-07:00","id":1126960,"title":"","content":"I like thinking Arcadia is missing &quot;actors&quot; and the Gentry kidnap humans to take part in their stories. I'm pretty sure Dave has said it's not, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:29:03-07:00","id":1127169,"title":"","content":"Sounds like I need to rethink my cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T08:08:08-07:00","id":1127642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1126960#post1126960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like thinking Arcadia is missing &quot;actors&quot; and the Gentry kidnap humans to take part in their stories. I'm pretty sure Dave has said it's not, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd wondered if it might be stability - everything functions only because of bargains between inhabitants, and humans are needed to make those concrete. But Dave has also said that the Gentry aren't native to Arcadia - they arrived later. (And some of them are still elsewhere).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T18:05:59-07:00","id":1127864,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah. I forgot he said that, too. I hope they do something with it in a supplement.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, don't changelings become true fae when their Clarity is low enough and Wyrd is high enough? So if Gentry are evolved changelings and changelings are originally human then it's no revelation to say the Gentry are foreigners to Arcadia. I thought<i> Imperial Mysteries</i> said they were in fact fallen from the Supernal, but that's a <i>Mage</i> supplement and, at any rate, I think that's been ret-conned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":". 08-12-2017, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T17:28:11-07:00","id":1131524,"title":"","content":"According to the current Changeling Devs the first Gentry exist because they made a deal with Arcadia to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T17:51:57-07:00","id":1131531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1127864#post1127864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Actually, don't changelings become true fae when their Clarity is low enough and Wyrd is high enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, getting your Wyrd as high as it would go was a prerequisite to tripping a narrative flag that started your Clarity on a fairly rapid slide downhill that culminated in you haring off to Arcadia to shed the last of your humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I thought<i> Imperial Mysteries</i> said they were in fact fallen from the Supernal, but that's a <i>Mage</i> supplement and, at any rate, I think that's been ret-conned. </div> </div> </div>Imperial Mysteries gave an example of weird Supernal entities in the form of the Old Gods of Thistle, who hit a lot of the same descriptive notes as the True Fae and are bizarrely persistent in not <i>staying</i> cast out from the Supernal despite the atemporal nature of the Exarchs' mythic war on the Heavens \u2014 they might or might not have been the Supernal bases of the Gentry, but what they definitely weren't was solid proof that the Strangers were cast-out Platonic forms from the dawn of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}